  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative led by Marcus Cole, launching in Q3 2023 with a kickoff on July 15th. The team is expanding with five new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, with onboarding sessions scheduled for September 10th and April 15th, 2023. Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption, effective January next year. The project is exploring a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology. Budgets have been approved for training ($15,000) and compliance ($55,000). Stakeholder feedback on the prototype is requested by the end of November, and a detailed assessment of similar projects is recommended."
